NAME
       installer - install PureC OS from the live medium to a disk

SYNOPSIS
       /sbin/installer

DESCRIPTION
       A console installer in the spirit of archinstall. Run it as root from
       the live system. It asks, in this order:

       disk       the whole disk is erased; type its name to confirm
       hostname, time zone
       root password
       users      any number up to 8 (or none), each with a password and an
                  "administrator" answer that puts the user into wheel (sudo)
       profile    1 console only, 2 graphical: the package "userspace" is
                  downloaded from its GitHub repository (asked for when it is
                  not in [trusted] of /etc/pkg/pkg.conf)
       packages   extra package names from /etc/pkg/pkg.conf

       Nothing is written before the summary is confirmed. Then the kernel
       writes a GPT (EFI system partition, ext2 root, swap on ATA/SATA disks),
       copies the live system and writes the accounts. After that the new
       partition is the running root, and the installer runs
       "mkinitcpio -u" (root=UUID= in limine.conf), installs the packages with
       pkg and sets /etc/init/default.target (graphical.target when the user
       space was installed, otherwise multi-user.target).

       Only /sbin/installer may write whole disks (the kernel gives the
       storage right by the program path).

FILES
       /etc/pkg/pkg.conf, /etc/init/default.target

SEE ALSO
       pkg(8), init(8), mkinitcpio(8), fdisk(8), sudo(8)
